body: "## Decision\n\nAccepted: keep `author` as the stable effective principal and record runtime observation separately as optional `agent_harness`, `agent_model`, `agent_model_source`, and `agent_session` history fields. Widening author to `harness:<harness>/<model>` is rejected because it breaks existing equality filters, increases cardinality, and conflates stable selection with volatile observation. Signed principals remain deferred to pm-u14c.\n\n## Contract\n\n- `agent_harness?: string`: normalized low-cardinality harness namespace. Missing means no bounded signal matched.\n- `agent_model?: string`: bounded model identifier exactly observed from an allowed signal. Missing means unknown and never changes the effective author to `unknown`.\n- `agent_model_source?: override | environment | mcp_client | argv`: fixed-cardinality provenance for the model value. It is absent whenever `agent_model` is absent.\n- `agent_session?: string`: bounded invocation identifier for local correlation. Missing means the host exposed no session signal.\n\nAuthor precedence remains explicit argument, `PM_AUTHOR`, configured default, detected harness, then `unknown`. Detection always executes independently, so asserted or configured authors may still carry observed agent fields. These observations are unverified claims: they are attribution/context only and MUST NOT authorize access, ownership takeover, or privileged operations.\n\n## Privacy and compatibility\n\nLocal append-only history may contain all four optional fields. Telemetry may emit only presence booleans at minimal capture, or installation-keyed one-way hashes of harness/model plus the fixed model-source enum at redacted/max capture. `agent_session` must never leave the machine. Legacy entries without these optional fields remain valid and replay/verifiability semantics are unchanged.\n\nAny field rename, author-string incorporation, cardinality expansion, session export, or authorization use requires an explicit superseding or amending Decision item linked to this ADR."
